>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `linarith_solver`

``` hol4
linarithLib.linarith_solver : TraverseExt.ssolver
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Provides the named unsafe simplifier solver `"lin_arith"`.

The solver proves arithmetic side conditions from the simplifier's
`context_thms` and the [global `[arith]` facts](#linarithData.arith), by
the same direct forward arithmetic, and the same cache (reset by
`linarithLib.clear_linarith_caches ()`), as
[`LINARITH_ss`](#linarithLib.LINARITH_ss). A proposition outside linear
arithmetic is proved only when the context, together with the `[arith]`
facts, is arithmetically contradictory; a context with no arithmetic in
it is declined, whatever facts are declared.

Solvers of this name, built with
[`linarith_solver_with_facts`](#linarithLib.linarith_solver_with_facts)
over the context's `[arith]` facts, are installed in the clasimp and
Aesop simpsets. One can be suppressed for one invocation with
[`simpExtLib.ExclX "solver:lin_arith"`](#simpExtLib.ExclX) or removed
with [`simpExtLib.remove_solver "lin_arith"`](#simpExtLib.remove_solver).
This solver can be added to another simpset with
[`simpExtLib.add_unsafe_solver`](#simpExtLib.add_unsafe_solver).

### Failure

The solver raises a `HOL_ERR` when its requested proposition does not
follow by supported direct linear arithmetic. The simplifier treats this
as the solver being inapplicable and may try another solver.

### Example

``` hol4
val arithmetic_ss =
  simpExtLib.add_unsafe_solver linarithLib.linarith_solver
    (simpExtLib.lift_simpset (BasicProvers.srw_ss ()));

Theorem linarith_solver_example:
  !x y z : num. x <= y /\ y <= z ==> x <= z
Proof
  rpt strip_tac >>
  simpExtLib.FULL_SIMP_TAC arithmetic_ss []
QED
```

